      "content": "That's an important distinction. If we're looking at it through the lens of predictive analytics, we're basically trying to understand risk profiles. \n\nLet's look at another pair to see if the pattern holds. If we have two students with identical academic records and minor behavioral notes, but one lives in a high-income area and the other in an area with higher rates of crime or poverty, wouldn't the predictive model naturally flag the second student as a higher risk for future disciplinary issues? I'm trying to see if the \"risk\" is essentially inherent to the environmental profile, even when the individual student's behavior has been perfectly fine so far.",
